The function `exchange` takes two lists of numbers as input. It checks if it is possible to exchange elements between the two lists to make all the elements of the first list to be even.

The function works by counting the number of odd numbers in the first list (`lst1`) and even numbers in the second list (`lst2`). If there are more or equal even numbers in `lst2` than odd numbers in `lst1`, it means that it is possible to exchange elements between the two lists to make all the elements of `lst1` to be even.

